# Phase 6: FastAPI Backend Integration Plan

The goal of this phase is to expose our powerful LangGraph-driven python application as a stateless/RESTful FastAPI backend. This will lay the groundwork for building the final Next.js React frontend.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - Replacing terminal `input()` with API calls means we have to refactor some of our Python scripts. Specifically, `src/onboarding.py` relies heavily on `input()`. We'll need to create an API-friendly version of onboarding.
> - For LangGraph's state to persist between API requests, we will use a **MemorySaver** (in-memory SQLite/Dictionary) as the LangGraph `checkpointer` for our MVP. Each user will have a `session_id`. When they send a `/chat` request, LangGraph will load their exact state using this `session_id`.
> - Please approve this plan before we start writing code.

