## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]  
> - **ChromaDB Concurrency:** Right now, ChromaDB saves to `./data/chroma_db`. If we test this API locally, multiple requests might trip over each other if editing Chroma sequentially. For MVP it should be completely fine, but are we okay keeping this locally on disk for now?
> - **Long-Term Memory:** Our `StudentProfileManager` (Insight Tracker) writes to `data/student_profile.json`. For the MVP, if multiple users connect, this single JSON will collide. We can fix this by prepending the `session_id` to the file (e.g., `data/{session_id}_profile.json`). Should we implement that safety boundary here?

